1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Can restoring functional BUBR1 improve chromosome segregation?

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
BUBR1 helps restrain APC/C–CDC20 until chromosome attachments are ready.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
This checkpoint protects daughter cells from receiving incorrect chromosome numbers.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:27,000
The case contains two BUB1B variants: p.Leu737Ter and p.Asn1002Lys.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:34,000
The stop can reduce full-length protein; N1002K changes the C-terminal domain.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Their phase is unresolved: both cis and trans configurations must be evaluated.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:47,000
AAT becomes AAG, replacing asparagine with lysine at residue 1002.

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:54,000
The longer, positively charged side chain changes local interaction possibilities.

9
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,000
This chemistry motivates a structural hypothesis; it does not establish dysfunction.

10
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,000
The wild-type model places N1002 in a locally confident structural region.

11
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Calculated solvent exposure and short polar contacts define its local environment.

12
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:20,000
We therefore test whether N1002K reduces the stable, functional protein pool.

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Our working mechanism is partial loss of function through altered stability or regulation.

14
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Reduced BUBR1 could weaken checkpoint control and PP2A-B56-dependent attachment regulation.

15
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:45,000
The predicted consequence is more chromosome-segregation errors: our primary functional endpoint.

16
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:53,000
We propose sodium phenylbutyrate, 4-PBA, as the lead repurposed candidate.

17
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:01,000
The premise: N1002K retains useful activity, but instability limits protein availability.

18
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Improved proteostasis could restore the stable pool and recover BUBR1-dependent control.

19
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:17,000
The predicted benefit is better chromosome segregation, beyond increased protein abundance.

20
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Rescue must occur at feasible exposure without expanding genomically unstable cells.

21
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:30,000
These predictions make 4-PBA our priority for functional testing.

22
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:37,000
NMN probes NAD+/SIRT2-dependent abundance; TUDCA offers another proteostasis hypothesis.

23
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Amlexanox separately tests readthrough of the p.Leu737Ter premature-stop allele.

24
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Test candidates separately in cells reproducing the confirmed genotype and allele phase.

25
00:02:53,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Advance the candidate that reproducibly restores segregation fidelity at non-toxic exposure.
